    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Design Notes\n\n- **Maximum Condensate Flow**: Achieved during plant start-up when pipes and equipment are heated up\n- **Design Rule**: The condensate load used to design condensate pipe lines should be **twice the maximum production load**\n- **Units**: SI Units (Pa/m, kg/h)\n\n## Equipment Piping and Condensate Load\n\nTypical maximum condensate load and equipment outlet pipe size:\n\n| Maximum Condensate Load (kg/h) | Outlet Pipe Size (mm, in) |\n|--------------------------------|---------------------------|\n| 200                            | 15 (1/2)                  |\n| 500                            | 20 (3/4)                  |\n| 1000                           | 25 (1)                    |\n| 2000                           | 32 (1 1/4)                |\n| 3000                           | 40 (1 1/2)                |\n| 5000                           | 50 (2)                    |\n| > 5000                         | 65 - 100 (2 1/2 - 4)      |"
    }
